Ryujinx shader IR: a new instruction for the Ampere front end's tensor-core path (tools/shaders/ampere/frontend/AmpereCoopMat.cs):
HMMA as one VK_KHR_cooperative_matrix multiply-add. Sources are the A, B and C registers (32-bit words), the destinations one word
per D register (a vector result, like TextureSample). Also Float16Arithmetic: one fp16 add, multiply or fused multiply-add
(Index 0, 1, 2) of fp32 operands that hold fp16 values, done in float16 (single rounding) and returned as fp32. The Ryujinx code in the context lines is MIT.
--- a/IntermediateRepresentation/Instruction.cs
+++ b/IntermediateRepresentation/Instruction.cs
@@ -125,6 +125,8 @@
         VoteAll,
         VoteAllEqual,
         VoteAny,
+        CooperativeMatrixMulAdd,   // Ampere front end: HMMA as a cooperative-matrix multiply-add (AmpereCoopMat.cs)
+        Float16Arithmetic,         // Ampere front end: one fp16 add/mul/fma in native float16 (Index: kind; AmpereCoopMat.cs)

         Count,

